  {
   "_key": "127bd1dabc40",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "029d4441c122",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "For a first trip to ancient Egypt: November, February, March. For a Nile cruise: November to February, or March and April on a dahabiya. For a Red Sea rest: October to May, or a dedicated summer beach trip. For the desert: October to March. For going deep in Luxor and Aswan, skip high summer."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
  },
  {
   "_key": "000000000057",
   "_type": "block",
   "children": [
    {
     "_key": "000000000056",
     "_type": "span",
     "marks": [],
     "text": "What matters in choosing the season is not average temperature alone. Where you walk, what hour you move, how crowded it will be, what the city looks like at night. Choosing with all of that in view makes Egypt much easier to travel."
    }
   ],
   "markDefs": [],
   "style": "normal"
